        "text": "<p>BLUETTI Elite 300 is built around a 3,014Wh LiFePO₄ battery system, making it suitable for powering refrigerators, medical devices, tools, and other high-demand appliances during outages or outdoor use. Its 2,400W continuous output (with higher surge capacity) allows it to run energy-intensive equipment like microwaves and heaters, positioning it as a serious alternative to traditional fuel generators for moderate loads. One of its key strengths is the balance between capacity and portability. While still heavy, it is notably more compact than many other 3kWh-class units, making it more practical for RVs, van life, and mobile work setups. Users and reviewers frequently highlight its solid build quality, efficient thermal management, and integrated LiFePO₄ chemistry, which is known for long cycle life and improved safety compared to older lithium-ion types.</p>",
